### [qlog](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-quic-qlog-00)
- **Presenter**: Lucas Pardue
- **Documents**: [`draft-ietf-quic-qlog-main-schema`](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-ietf-quic-qlog-main-schema/), [`draft-ietf-quic-qlog-quic-events`](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-ietf-quic-qlog-quic-events/), [`draft-ietf-quic-qlog-h3-events`](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-ietf-quic-qlog-h3-events/)
- **Technical Overview & Proposals**:
  - **TLS Layering Cleanup**: Proposal to strip TLS-specific logging fields/events (e.g., SNI, ALPN, cipher suite, resumption booleans) from the core QUIC qlog schema. TLS logging will be split into a separate TLS qlog extension draft (Christian Huitema volunteered to co-author).
  - **Tuple & Path ID**: `tuple_id` will be moved exclusively to packet events (`packet_sent`, `packet_received`, `packet_dropped`) rather than generic event headers. Core qlog will avoid adding multipath events or path IDs. Yanmei Liu and Christian Huitema volunteered to work on a separate multipath qlog draft.
  - **`connection_id_updated` Event**: Proposal to delete this event from the core schema as it is redundant with packet headers and tuple assignment events.
- **Discussion**:
  - Christian Huitema and Martin Duke supported removing TLS parameters from the QUIC core logging schema to keep protocol boundaries clean.
  - General support was expressed for simplifying core qlog events to accelerate finalization.

