### [Receive timestamps](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-quic-receive-timestamps-01)
- **Presenter**: Marten Seemann
- **Document**: [`draft-ietf-quic-receive-ts`](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-ietf-quic-receive-ts/)
- **Technical Overview**:
  - Updates include range encoding changes (`additional_timestamp_delta_count` starting at 0 for 1 delta), new transport parameter code points, explicit protocol violation error definitions, and decode safety bounds.
  - Implementation status: Supported in MsQuic (v0.3/v0.4) and Google Quiche (v0.4); Chrome deployment planned for Q1 with BBR integration.
- **Discussion**:
  - Magnus Westerlund requested clearer specification text regarding local microsecond clock assumptions and ACK frequency interactions.
  - Yanmei Liu confirmed positive results when integrating receive timestamps into congestion controllers.
  - Draft is nearing readiness for WGLC pending minor text updates.

