### [QUIC NAT Traversal](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-quic-quic-nat-traversal-00)
- **Presenter**: Marten Seemann
- **Document**: `draft-seemann-quic-nat-traversal`
- **Technical Overview**:
  - Proposes peer-to-peer QUIC hole punching built upon MASQUE `Connect-UDP` relay channels and connection migration primitives.
  - Introduces an `ALTERNATIVE_ADDRESS` frame allowing servers to communicate candidate addresses post-handshake, enabling background hole punching without delaying initial connection setup.
- **Discussion**:
  - Aldi Sefa, Antonio Gurtov, Nidhi Jaju, Eric Kinnear, Ben Schwartz, Stefano Fogliata, Marco Munizaga, Lorenzo Colitti, and Gorry Fairhurst discussed use cases (e.g., AirDrop, P2P file sharing), local network privacy implications, stateful firewalls vs. NATs, and coordination across IETF and W3C.

